## Why This Problem Is Asked
This problem combines prefix DP with an inner backward sweep to compute the optimal segment ending at each position. It tests understanding of state decomposition, reconstruction logic, and handles edge cases like negative values naturally.

## Key Concepts
- DP state: dp[i][t] tracks the optimal value using the first i elements with t segments
- Inner loop: expanding the left boundary computes segment maximum on the fly
- Reconstruction: store predecessor pointers to recover exact subarray boundaries
- Complexity: O(n²k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueSubarrays(A, k) {
    const n = A.length;
    const dp = Array(n + 1).fill(null).map(() => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
    const prev = Array(n + 1).fill(null).map(() => Array(k + 1).fill(0));
    dp[0][0] = 0;

    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
            let curMax = -Infinity;
            for (let l = i; l >= 1; l--) {
                curMax = Math.max(curMax, A[l - 1]);
                const val = (dp[l - 1][t - 1] !== -Infinity ? dp[l - 1][t - 1] + curMax : -Infinity);
                if (val > dp[i][t]) {
                    dp[i][t] = val;
                    prev[i][t] = l;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    const result = [];
    let i = n, t = k;
    while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
        const l = prev[i][t];
        result.unshift([l, i]);
        i = l - 1;
        t--;
    }
    return { value: dp[n][k], boundaries: result };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Scheduling perspective: minimize peak workload across days; the DP is a straightforward partition DP with a range max cost. It tests understanding of maintaining running max within inner loop and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes
- Range max within an inner loop
- Path reconstruction via cut[]
- Edge cases: empty input, large n, identical durations

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(L){
  const n=L.length;
  const dp=new Array(n+1).fill(Infinity);
  const cut=new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  dp[0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    let curMax=0;
    for(let k=1;k<=i;k++){
      curMax = Math.max(curMax, L[i-k]);
      const val = dp[i-k] + curMax;
      if(val < dp[i]){ dp[i] = val; cut[i] = k; }
    }
  }
  const days=[];
  let i=n;
  while(i>0){
    const k=cut[i];
    days.push(L.slice(i-k, i));
    i -= k;
  }
  days.reverse();
  return {cost: dp[n], days};
}
```

